# Scripts verification

After implementing features, fixes, or refactors that affect source, configs, or tests — verify with the matching scripts from `@package.json` before considering the work done.

## When to run

| When                                                                    | Command              |
| ----------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------- |
| Changes under `src` or verification configs (eslint, tsconfig, steiger) | `yarn check`         |
| Unit tests or tested logic touched                                      | also `yarn test`     |
| E2E specs or a critical user flow touched                               | also `yarn test:e2e` |

Skip only when the change cannot affect these checks (e.g. Cursor rules / docs-only with no `src` impact), and say so briefly.

## Do not run automatically

Do not auto-run: `format`, `format:check`, `lint:fix`, `test:watch`, `test:e2e:ui` (write / interactive / redundant with `yarn check`).

## How to verify

1. From the project root, run the commands from the matrix above that match the change.
2. If a command fails, fix the issue and re-run until clean (or until remaining failures are explicitly deferred by the user).
3. Report briefly which scripts ran and the result.

## Preferences

- Prefer fixing failures over skipping or weakening checks.
- `yarn check` already includes lint + Steiger + typecheck; do not duplicate a full Steiger-only run unless the change is structural-only and `fsd-steiger-verify` applies in isolation.
